BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Visiting Artist Talk - Debra Priestly
DTSTART:20261014T200000
DTEND:20261014T210000
DTSTAMP:20261014T155139Z
UID:8f28fcfc7c2fa40f0fec05689efe6c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Debra Priestly is a visual artist exploring themes of memory\,
  ancestry\, history\, and cultural preservation. Her work is widely exhibi
 ted and part of numerous collections\, including the Albany Institute of H
 istory and Art\, the Francis Greenburger Collection\, the Pennsylvania Aca
 demy of the Fine Arts\, the Schomburg Center for Research in Black Culture
 \, the Sandor Family Collection\, and the Petrucci Family Foundation Colle
 ction. It has appeared in Art in America\, BOMB magazine\, dART Internatio
 nal\, The New York Times\, and other publications. Awards include two New 
 York Foundation for the Arts Fellowships in Painting\, Art Omi Residency\,
  The Marie Walsh Sharpe’s The Space Program Residency\, and the Elizabet
 h Foundation for the Arts Robert Blackburn Printmaking Workshop Studio Imm
 ersion Project Fellowship. She holds an MFA from Pratt Institute and a BFA
  from The Ohio State University. Priestly lives and works in New York City
  and Upstate New York. She taught art at various institutions\, including 
 Sarah Lawrence College\, The Cooper Union for the Advancement of Science a
 nd Art\, and Queens College\, City University of New York\, where she was 
 recently designated Professor Emerita.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Studio Center\, 80 Pearl Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/visiting-a
 rtist-talk-debra-priestly-08-10-2026-11-18-58
END:VEVENT
